WEBVTT

00:11.510 --> 00:13.530
Scent of decaying roses...

00:13.880 --> 00:17.280
Sea that swallows the light of the
setting sun as the black dog howls...

00:17.800 --> 00:21.530
With the mingling of black and
white, souls vanish into chaos!

00:21.530 --> 00:24.540
Take this! Grade 5 Magic:

00:26.040 --> 00:28.040
Prismatic Missile!

00:39.530 --> 00:40.640
Did that work?

00:49.480 --> 00:52.610
Scourge of light,
burn the evil ones to ash!

00:52.910 --> 00:56.030
Grade 5 Magic: Thunderbolt!

01:02.930 --> 01:04.430
(Thunderbolt)

01:12.270 --> 01:13.970
We still can't bring it down?

01:13.970 --> 01:15.970
But right now...

01:15.970 --> 01:18.490
Go, Marina! Cut off its head!

01:18.490 --> 01:20.030
I'm on it!

01:20.840 --> 01:22.520
Critical Weapon!

01:22.870 --> 01:23.950
(Critical Weapon)

01:23.970 --> 01:25.530
Magic Blade!

01:51.980 --> 01:54.880
We... We did it...

02:03.250 --> 02:04.980
And he's down.

02:04.980 --> 02:06.640
Thank you for watching.

02:06.960 --> 02:08.470
End stream.

02:18.170 --> 02:25.140
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

03:40.000 --> 03:42.050
(Episode 3: Overflow)

03:42.050 --> 03:43.520
(Episode 3: Overflow)
They beat a Zarnag?!

03:43.520 --> 03:45.670
(Episode 3: Overflow)
What was that rainbow-colored spell?

03:45.670 --> 03:47.060
Some undiscovered type of magic?

03:47.060 --> 03:49.420
Awesome! What was this party called again?

03:49.420 --> 03:50.610
Clover!

03:51.540 --> 03:52.710
Whoa...

03:53.520 --> 03:53.540
- We did it!

03:53.540 --> 03:55.050
- I probably used too much mana there.
- We did it!

03:55.050 --> 03:56.480
- I probably used too much mana there.
- We did!

03:56.480 --> 03:58.610
- When it went from Yuke's "snap" to
Silk's "kaboom" to Rain's "zap, zap,"

03:58.610 --> 04:02.780
- That was a battle far too tough to expect
a bunch of newbie adventurers to fight.
- When it went from Yuke's "snap" to
Silk's "kaboom" to Rain's "zap, zap,"

04:02.780 --> 04:03.450
- that was so amazing!

04:03.450 --> 04:04.280
- This stream might put some
wind in those girls' sails,
- that was so amazing!

04:04.280 --> 04:06.310
- This stream might put some
wind in those girls' sails,
- You guys aren't hurt, right?

04:06.310 --> 04:08.100
- This stream might put some
wind in those girls' sails,
- We're both fine. It was so much fun!

04:08.100 --> 04:10.080
- but for me, it was video-proof
of my own mistakes.
- We're both fine. It was so much fun!

04:10.080 --> 04:11.290
- but for me, it was video-proof
of my own mistakes.
- Thanks!

04:11.850 --> 04:13.370
Good work.

04:13.370 --> 04:15.680
You three can expect
a lecture from me later.

04:15.680 --> 04:17.430
What? Harsh!

04:17.430 --> 04:21.690
Yeah... but I'm going to lecture you, too.

04:21.690 --> 04:22.690
Why me?!

04:23.140 --> 04:25.700
You went in there intending
to die, didn't you?

04:26.860 --> 04:30.950
I have a few things I'd like to say
about the instructions you gave, too!

04:30.950 --> 04:32.050
Me, too!

04:32.050 --> 04:33.700
It's three against one?

04:35.090 --> 04:39.610
Just make sure you understand
that we only won by pure luck.

04:40.740 --> 04:42.830
Okay, okay. How about a compromise?

04:42.830 --> 04:44.710
We'll all review what happened together.

04:47.720 --> 04:49.500
Wow, it's gorgeous!

04:49.500 --> 04:52.350
I'd love to wash the sweat off.

04:52.860 --> 04:55.490
I'll be over there getting our camp ready.

04:55.490 --> 04:57.980
Go on and wash off the sweat...

04:58.570 --> 04:59.770
and the Zarnag blood.

04:59.770 --> 05:00.910
Right...

05:00.910 --> 05:01.710
Okay.

05:04.970 --> 05:06.320
I'm first!

05:07.220 --> 05:09.750
Rain, Silk! Hurry up!

05:10.660 --> 05:12.580
This feels great!

05:15.280 --> 05:16.450
Camping out, huh?

05:17.090 --> 05:18.330
This brings back memories...

05:18.810 --> 05:19.050
(Six Months Ago)

05:19.050 --> 05:21.340
(Six Months Ago)
of the preliminary adventurer course.

05:21.340 --> 05:22.070
(Six Months Ago)

05:22.610 --> 05:24.340
Okay, looking good.

05:25.020 --> 05:27.130
You guys have a knack for this.

05:27.130 --> 05:29.590
You're sure to get passing
scores if you can keep this up.

05:29.590 --> 05:31.290
All right!

05:31.290 --> 05:34.360
If there are any areas in which we
can improve, please let us know.

05:34.360 --> 05:34.870
Yeah.

05:34.870 --> 05:37.100
Well, if I had to say...

05:37.710 --> 05:40.100
Marina, you can be a bit sloppy.

05:40.100 --> 05:42.120
Silk, you're too careful.

05:43.050 --> 05:46.100
And Rain, you could stand to
assert yourself a bit more.

05:46.100 --> 05:48.860
Okay. Got it.

05:49.400 --> 05:52.570
But if I were the guild official
in charge,

05:52.570 --> 05:56.870
I'd be presenting you all with D-rank
adventurer licenses right now.

05:59.550 --> 06:01.000
The tent's up!

06:01.360 --> 06:04.340
We've gathered firewood and
set up an alarm, too.

06:04.860 --> 06:06.980
I'll take care of dinner!

06:06.980 --> 06:10.230
I'm gonna make a soup from the
Horned Rabbit we caught today!

06:10.230 --> 06:12.680
We'll be counting on you, then. Rain?

06:12.680 --> 06:14.350
Yep. I'm on it.

06:14.730 --> 06:16.350
Water, come forth!

06:16.830 --> 06:18.390
Create Water!

06:18.390 --> 06:20.100
(Create Water)

06:20.100 --> 06:23.100
Thanks, Rain! I'll whip this up quick!

06:23.100 --> 06:25.000
Flames, ignite!

06:25.000 --> 06:25.950
Tinder!

06:26.710 --> 06:27.710
(Tinder)

06:27.730 --> 06:28.210
- They look like they'll make
a pretty well-balanced party.

06:28.210 --> 06:29.480
- Still awesome!
- They look like they'll make
a pretty well-balanced party.

06:29.480 --> 06:31.250
- Now, let's put these in the pot, too.
- They look like they'll make
a pretty well-balanced party.

06:31.250 --> 06:31.740
- Yeah.
- They look like they'll make
a pretty well-balanced party.

06:32.320 --> 06:34.230
- They might overtake Thunder Pike before long.

06:34.230 --> 06:36.350
- Let's put this in, too.
- They might overtake Thunder Pike before long.

06:37.440 --> 06:37.460
- It smells good.

06:37.460 --> 06:38.460
- I hope all of your adventures
will be full of happiness.
- It smells good.

06:38.460 --> 06:39.190
- I hope all of your adventures
will be full of happiness.
- Right?

06:39.190 --> 06:41.590
- I hope all of your adventures
will be full of happiness.
- All the spices we put in are the perfect accent.

06:41.590 --> 06:42.350
- All the spices we put in are the perfect accent.

06:43.170 --> 06:47.380
I never thought I'd end
up in a party with them.

06:48.180 --> 06:50.620
You really never know what's
gonna happen in life.

06:51.740 --> 06:54.240
(Several Days Later)

06:54.570 --> 06:59.850
Yuke, what do you think the
guild master wanted to see us about?

06:59.850 --> 07:02.270
Most likely the Zarnag.

07:02.270 --> 07:03.520
But why?

07:03.970 --> 07:09.230
That quest should have
been offered as rank B,

07:09.230 --> 07:11.530
but the guild threw it at a D-rank party.

07:11.530 --> 07:13.910
That might be how it appears, anyway.

07:14.710 --> 07:17.370
We'll probably be praised for
getting rid of the Zarnag,

07:17.370 --> 07:19.910
but he might have some more
troubling things to say, too.

07:21.140 --> 07:22.260
(Finis Adventurer's Guild
Guild Master Benwood)

07:22.260 --> 07:23.600
(Finis Adventurer's Guild
Guild Master Benwood)
Thanks for waiting.

07:29.150 --> 07:31.260
You've done it this time, Yuke.

07:31.610 --> 07:33.260
It's not my fault.

07:33.260 --> 07:35.690
Tell me what happened in detail.

07:35.690 --> 07:37.320
The details are exactly as I reported.

07:37.320 --> 07:40.390
I'm not asking for the objective
record you submitted.

07:40.960 --> 07:43.770
I'm asking you to give me
your thoughts on the matter.

07:44.780 --> 07:47.530
Stop it! Enough with the
intimidation, Benwood!

07:47.530 --> 07:49.120
You're scaring them!

07:49.120 --> 07:52.530
And if you wanted to talk to me,
then you should've called just me here!

07:52.960 --> 07:55.660
Master, this is the guild master!

08:01.870 --> 08:05.270
Good. You've dropped that
unnecessarily polite tone.

08:05.270 --> 08:09.160
That hurts! You're as aggravating
as ever, aren't you?

08:09.160 --> 08:10.670
The way you act is so crude!

08:13.360 --> 08:16.010
Sit down. You girls, too.

08:17.440 --> 08:20.010
If this is about the Zarnag,
my report says it all.

08:20.760 --> 08:22.810
So how does it look to you?

08:24.110 --> 08:26.570
It may be an Overflow.

08:26.570 --> 08:28.310
It should be investigated at once.

08:28.700 --> 08:29.790
I see.

08:30.630 --> 08:33.190
I'll issue an emergency
investigation quest.

08:34.320 --> 08:37.070
Yuke, what's an Overflow?

08:37.070 --> 08:40.950
It's when some catalyst causes
monsters to overflow from dungeons.

08:41.360 --> 08:45.710
Monsters' lives are bound to
the mana found in dungeons.

08:45.710 --> 08:50.640
But sometimes, that shackle comes loose
and they're able to leave the dungeon.

08:50.640 --> 08:53.460
It's also evidence of a Stampede.

08:53.460 --> 08:54.810
Stampede?

08:54.810 --> 08:56.990
You mean when monsters go on a rampage...

08:56.990 --> 09:00.850
...and wash over towns like a tsunami?

09:01.690 --> 09:06.100
If monsters like that Zarnag are
getting out of their dungeons...

09:06.100 --> 09:09.810
All right. We'll take care
of the investigation.

09:09.810 --> 09:12.560
And I must say this to all of you:

09:13.480 --> 09:19.240
I sincerely apologize for exposing
you to such terrible danger.

09:19.240 --> 09:22.490
U-Um, we were just fine, really.

09:22.490 --> 09:23.700
We had Yuke, after all.

09:23.700 --> 09:27.140
Yes, that's right! We had no
problems since he was there!

09:27.140 --> 09:29.870
Yuke's magic basically defeated it.

09:30.260 --> 09:33.550
Yuke aside, that stream proved to me

09:33.550 --> 09:37.750
that you three are
plenty capable yourselves.

09:37.750 --> 09:39.510
With that in mind,

09:39.510 --> 09:43.010
I'd like to promote you to
rank C. What do you think?

09:43.680 --> 09:45.340
A-Are you sure?

09:45.340 --> 09:48.390
I thought this was going to
turn into a big cover-up...

09:48.390 --> 09:51.270
This was a decision reached after
discussion among the guild branches.

09:51.820 --> 09:55.650
It is contingent on having the A-rank
adventurer Yuke assisting them.

09:55.970 --> 09:58.620
Come on, have you gone senile?

09:58.620 --> 09:59.920
I'm B-rank.

09:59.920 --> 10:02.280
Don't be silly.
That spell in your stream...

10:02.660 --> 10:07.300
Wasn't that Prismatic Missile,
a new spell nobody else knows?

10:07.300 --> 10:10.290
I've made sure everyone knows
you slayed the Zarnag with it.

10:10.650 --> 10:11.540
Huh?

10:11.540 --> 10:15.290
Congratulations! Starting
today, you're an A-ranker!

10:15.290 --> 10:17.550
Here! Just sign this!

10:19.850 --> 10:21.600
Congrats!

10:21.600 --> 10:22.930
Congratulations.

10:22.930 --> 10:25.430
Rank A is truly incredible!

10:25.760 --> 10:29.180
Thanks. Congrats on your
promotion to rank C, too.

10:29.490 --> 10:30.650
Thanks!

10:30.650 --> 10:32.170
Thank you.

10:32.170 --> 10:33.440
Thank you!

10:33.850 --> 10:37.570
That was rough, but I'm
glad we got the job done.

10:37.570 --> 10:38.820
And that's our reward.

10:39.340 --> 10:42.010
Silk, check the contents for us.

10:42.010 --> 10:44.650
It should be a big step
toward buying our base.

10:44.650 --> 10:46.330
Please excuse me, then.

10:48.270 --> 10:50.190
It's so much...

10:52.020 --> 10:56.890
This quest ended up being
treated as B-rank,

10:56.890 --> 10:59.460
and I sold the Zarnag's
body for a nice profit.

11:00.410 --> 11:02.220
That's the last one...

11:04.530 --> 11:07.350
Um, Master, this is addressed to you.

11:11.610 --> 11:13.600
An apology from me.

11:13.920 --> 11:16.730
That Benwood never changes.

11:16.730 --> 11:18.380
I accept it with gratitude.

11:18.380 --> 11:19.860
A Randall Platinum Coin?!

11:19.860 --> 11:21.740
Wow! I've never seen one before!

11:22.950 --> 11:26.240
Let's see...
I think we've reached our goal!

11:26.240 --> 11:27.870
We have enough money?!

11:29.060 --> 11:31.540
We've reached the amount
we'd planned to save.

11:31.540 --> 11:33.120
That's great! Congrats!

11:33.710 --> 11:38.940
But this was only possible thanks
to your help, so I do apologize.

11:38.940 --> 11:42.030
We never could have done this on our own.

11:42.030 --> 11:43.380
Silk.

11:43.800 --> 11:47.050
I'm the leader of Clover now.

11:47.050 --> 11:48.640
You don't have to put me on a pedestal.

11:49.430 --> 11:51.890
I'll do everything I can to help you guys,

11:52.270 --> 11:54.750
and the results of that belong to Clover.

11:54.750 --> 11:57.400
We all earned this together.

11:57.960 --> 12:00.020
Yes, you're right.

12:00.500 --> 12:02.280
Okay! Now, let's drink!

12:06.040 --> 12:07.560
Say, Yuke...

12:08.780 --> 12:11.290
What is your dream?

12:11.290 --> 12:12.410
Where'd that come from?

12:13.910 --> 12:18.000
The goal we set for ourselves
is within our reach now.

12:18.000 --> 12:21.170
I want to know what your dream
is so we can set our next goal.

12:22.310 --> 12:23.900
Well... okay.

12:26.080 --> 12:27.320
My dream is...

12:27.850 --> 12:30.550
to take on the deepest floor of
the dungeon Achromatic Darkness.

12:32.890 --> 12:34.310
A-Are you okay?!

12:34.670 --> 12:35.850
Isn't that...

12:36.330 --> 12:38.150
It's a dungeon with an Abyss Gate.

12:38.150 --> 12:40.000
Abyss Gate...

12:40.000 --> 12:46.810
A fixed artifact known as a
gateway to the underworld.

12:46.810 --> 12:51.200
And the only dungeon that's
been confirmed to have one...

12:51.200 --> 12:53.790
...is Achromatic Darkness?

12:53.790 --> 12:57.300
Do you want to go through an Abyss Gate?

12:57.300 --> 12:58.170
No.

12:58.570 --> 13:01.910
I want to see the edge of this
world that goes on forever

13:02.570 --> 13:04.070
with my own two eyes.

13:05.520 --> 13:08.210
An uncle of mine that I respect a lot

13:08.210 --> 13:10.470
once took on Achromatic Darkness.

13:11.060 --> 13:14.130
He wasn't able to conquer
the dungeon in the end,

13:15.060 --> 13:18.890
but after hearing the story over
and over again since I was little,

13:18.890 --> 13:22.190
I started to think
I wanted to try it someday.

13:22.590 --> 13:25.820
It's not so much a dream,
more of... a romantic idea.

13:26.090 --> 13:28.740
I think I kinda get it, though.

13:28.740 --> 13:32.450
Hey, Yuke, let's go there
and livestream it!

13:32.710 --> 13:36.250
Whoa, now. It's not that easy.

13:36.250 --> 13:40.530
Just entering Achromatic Darkness
requires permission from the government.

13:40.530 --> 13:43.210
It would take an A-rank party,
at the very least.

13:43.210 --> 13:45.310
I'm in.

13:45.310 --> 13:48.470
No, I think that should be our next goal.

13:48.780 --> 13:52.340
I also think your dream
is fantastic, Master!

13:52.700 --> 13:55.070
We'll work a lot harder!

13:55.070 --> 13:57.110
Let's make your dream come true!

13:57.110 --> 14:00.010
Yeah. It's our turn now.

14:00.010 --> 14:01.790
Let's do our best, Master!

14:01.790 --> 14:03.110
Whoa, whoa...

14:05.960 --> 14:10.490
Okay, then. Let's all go see the
Abyss Gate together someday.

14:10.490 --> 14:11.860
As Clover!

14:11.860 --> 14:13.240
See the Abyss Gate...

14:14.620 --> 14:16.080
As Clover!

14:19.330 --> 14:24.240
So Clover, the party that had all your
eyes glued to that Zarnag battle,

14:24.240 --> 14:27.340
is stirring us all up
again with a new stream!

14:28.060 --> 14:28.320
Their leader, Yuke the Red Mage, is legit amazing!

14:28.320 --> 14:29.570
(Enhanced Arm Strength,
Enhanced Stamina, Enhanced Leg Strength)
Their leader, Yuke the Red Mage, is legit amazing!

14:29.570 --> 14:31.090
Their leader, Yuke the Red
Mage, is legit amazing!

14:31.090 --> 14:32.470
- You can't navigate a battle like
this without tons of experience!

14:32.470 --> 14:33.820
- Marina, get back!
- You can't navigate a battle like
this without tons of experience!

14:33.820 --> 14:35.580
(Ice Magnet)
- You can't navigate a battle like
this without tons of experience!

14:35.600 --> 14:36.690
Protection!

14:36.690 --> 14:38.070
Protector Shield!

14:38.580 --> 14:40.580
(Protection)
(Protector Shield)

14:45.300 --> 14:47.530
Purify the evil ones!

14:47.530 --> 14:50.360
Grade 4 Magic: Lightning!

14:52.130 --> 14:53.390
(Lightning)

14:53.410 --> 14:54.910
For good measure...

14:54.910 --> 14:57.940
Check! Scroll of Rock Breaks!

14:58.390 --> 15:00.890
(Scroll of Rock Breaks)

15:03.300 --> 15:05.560
Yeah! We beat it!

15:05.560 --> 15:07.570
Thank you for watching.

15:07.570 --> 15:09.240
This has been Clover.

15:09.920 --> 15:14.680
In the month since they got together,
Clover has been a nonstop sensation!

15:16.280 --> 15:18.570
How does a useless idiot
who's so boring in every way,

15:18.570 --> 15:21.310
except for his looks,
suddenly get so popular?

15:21.700 --> 15:25.280
For a stream recorded so near the
surface to be this well-received...

15:25.280 --> 15:28.820
The quality of the viewers
has seriously declined.

15:29.230 --> 15:33.320
Yuke's getting cocky after getting
himself into a low-ranking party.

15:33.320 --> 15:36.880
I heard he was promoted
to rank A recently.

15:36.880 --> 15:39.050
Can't blame him for getting cocky.

15:39.050 --> 15:40.950
I'm more concerned about us.

15:41.580 --> 15:46.060
Thunder Pike has been screwing up constantly
due to poor-quality new members.

15:46.060 --> 15:49.340
None of them even stick around for long.

15:49.870 --> 15:55.450
I'd heard there were more loser adventurers
with a lack of drive, guts, and patience lately.

15:55.450 --> 15:58.010
I guess the rumors were true, huh?

15:58.320 --> 16:00.010
What a predicament.

16:00.660 --> 16:01.840
Where's Jamie?

16:01.840 --> 16:03.540
Not in the mood to drink, she said.

16:03.540 --> 16:06.570
Tch! She's never around these days.

16:06.570 --> 16:08.900
Even when we do quests,
she keeps slowing us down.

16:08.900 --> 16:10.940
She's just selfish.

16:10.940 --> 16:12.010
For good measure...

16:12.010 --> 16:15.150
Check! Scroll of Rock Breaks!

16:15.150 --> 16:16.970
Yeah! We beat it!

16:16.970 --> 16:19.160
Thank you for watching.

16:19.160 --> 16:21.110
This has been Clover.

16:21.790 --> 16:26.460
In the month since they got together,
Clover has been a nonstop sensation!

16:28.130 --> 16:28.920
Refill!

16:29.290 --> 16:30.130
Hurry it up!

16:30.130 --> 16:32.010
One moment, please.

16:32.010 --> 16:33.640
Bunch of half-wits.

16:34.420 --> 16:34.920
Hey...

16:35.400 --> 16:37.820
Why don't we ask him to come back?

16:37.820 --> 16:38.910
Yuke?

16:38.910 --> 16:39.550
Yeah.

16:40.120 --> 16:43.060
In spite of everything, he did
manage to keep up with us.

16:43.060 --> 16:45.660
At the very least, when he was with us,

16:45.660 --> 16:49.060
we didn't fail quests
continuously like this.

16:49.450 --> 16:52.340
Hmph. For being a chore boy,

16:52.340 --> 16:56.450
maybe he actually was... useful to us.

16:57.010 --> 16:59.310
The problem was the money, right?

16:59.310 --> 17:01.750
Let's just increase his cut a little.

17:01.750 --> 17:04.580
We can give Jamie a little less,
since she's been so useless.

17:05.690 --> 17:09.960
This might be the kind of situation
where it benefits us to give in.

17:09.960 --> 17:13.210
We can let bygones be bygones.

17:16.100 --> 17:18.470
We finally made it back!

17:18.860 --> 17:21.700
I misread the time when the
stagecoach would come by.

17:21.700 --> 17:22.470
Sorry, guys.

17:22.940 --> 17:25.100
Walking home was fun, too.

17:25.360 --> 17:29.950
Yeah. I think you have what
it takes to be a Bard, Yuke.

17:29.950 --> 17:34.110
I hope you'll tell us lots more stories.

17:34.490 --> 17:35.410
Sure.

17:35.410 --> 17:39.360
For now, let's report our
quest completion to the guild.

17:39.870 --> 17:42.090
You think Mamar's still there?

17:42.090 --> 17:43.870
Did you need to see her for something?

17:43.870 --> 17:45.610
I just wondered.

17:45.610 --> 17:48.250
You and her get along
pretty well, don't you?

17:48.250 --> 17:52.200
Well, I've known her ever
since I became an adventurer.

17:52.200 --> 17:56.000
Despite how she looks, she's the
most senior employee at this guild.

17:56.510 --> 17:59.060
Ask any adventurer in
your parents' generation.

17:59.060 --> 18:02.640
They'll tell you all you want to
know about Mamar the Grey Hermit.

18:03.050 --> 18:04.760
That's surprising...

18:04.760 --> 18:06.640
Why did you ask about Mamar?

18:06.640 --> 18:08.240
I-I just—

18:08.240 --> 18:09.640
Marina is jealous.

18:09.640 --> 18:12.140
Huh?! I-It's not like that!

18:12.140 --> 18:13.980
It's not! It's not, okay?!

18:13.980 --> 18:15.150
Huh?

18:18.450 --> 18:20.280
Hey there, Yuke.

18:23.120 --> 18:26.530
You three, go on inside and see Mamar.

18:32.690 --> 18:34.170
What do you want, Simon?

18:34.500 --> 18:36.660
Just to talk a bit.

18:36.660 --> 18:38.090
But not on our feet.

18:38.090 --> 18:39.350
Care for a drink?

18:39.350 --> 18:41.180
I just got back from a dungeon,
and I'm tired.

18:41.650 --> 18:43.800
I'll have to decline.

18:43.800 --> 18:45.220
Hold it!

18:47.730 --> 18:51.100
Yuke, why don't you come
back to Thunder Pike?

18:51.430 --> 18:52.480
What?!

18:56.480 --> 18:58.800
You already want to, right?

19:00.160 --> 19:01.490
I mean, don't you?

19:02.370 --> 19:04.990
To fulfill the dream you've been
talking about since we were kids,

19:05.530 --> 19:09.090
to take on the Abyss Gate
at the edge of the world...

19:10.250 --> 19:14.150
you need permission from both the
government and the Adventurer's Guild.

19:14.150 --> 19:19.000
You basically have to be a member
of an A-rank party like us.

19:20.760 --> 19:25.590
So I'm saying I'll let you
come back to Thunder Pike.

19:25.590 --> 19:27.640
I'll even reconsider your cut—

19:28.240 --> 19:30.020
Sorry, but I'm not interested.

19:30.020 --> 19:31.020
What?

19:31.340 --> 19:33.980
I'm the leader of Clover.

19:33.980 --> 19:35.380
I won't go back.

19:35.380 --> 19:40.080
You know, we've been through a lot
of trouble because you bailed on us!

19:40.080 --> 19:41.650
You don't feel bad about that?

19:42.220 --> 19:45.150
You said you understood and that
you wouldn't suffer without me.

19:45.150 --> 19:46.530
Quit trying to trip me up!

19:47.050 --> 19:47.950
What's that about?

19:47.950 --> 19:48.660
Sad...

19:48.660 --> 19:51.370
The fact is,
it's been a huge problem for us.

19:51.370 --> 19:54.250
We need you to
take responsibility for that.

19:54.250 --> 19:57.990
As an adventurer and as an adult,
it's just the right thing to do!

19:57.990 --> 20:01.920
How can you say that after
disrespecting me for so long?

20:02.250 --> 20:05.490
You think you can get away with it
because we were friends as kids?

20:06.430 --> 20:09.230
I have no intention of
returning to Thunder Pike.

20:09.230 --> 20:10.430
End of discussion.

20:10.430 --> 20:13.910
You're letting those
rookie girls deceive you!

20:13.910 --> 20:15.310
They're using you!

20:16.100 --> 20:19.600
You guys are the ones who used me.

20:20.150 --> 20:21.690
Later, Simon.

20:22.060 --> 20:25.350
Don't get cocky! You'll regret it!

20:37.430 --> 20:38.730
You heard, huh?

20:38.730 --> 20:40.410
Who was that guy?

20:40.410 --> 20:42.460
The leader of my former party.

20:42.880 --> 20:44.210
Are you going back to them?!

20:45.490 --> 20:48.430
D-Don't worry! I'm not
going back! You know that!

20:48.430 --> 20:49.670
Really?

20:50.190 --> 20:51.470
Really?!

20:51.850 --> 20:54.980
C-Could you just... let go of me first?

20:56.960 --> 20:59.450
It's okay. I'm not going back.

20:59.450 --> 21:00.980
I'm Clover's leader.

21:03.070 --> 21:04.320
Did you make that report?

21:04.320 --> 21:06.610
Oh... We were just about to. I'm sorry.

21:08.030 --> 21:10.060
Let's all go see Mamar together.

21:10.560 --> 21:11.240
When we're done—

21:11.240 --> 21:12.990
We'll go get drinks!

21:13.350 --> 21:16.370
Yeah, I do kinda feel like a round or two.

21:16.370 --> 21:17.750
I can drink in good spirits.

21:17.750 --> 21:20.560
Well, then, let's go see Mamar right now!

21:20.560 --> 21:22.400
Hey, no pushing! Come on!

21:22.400 --> 21:23.540
Let's go, Master!

21:23.560 --> 21:25.210
- Come on, hurry!
- I'm coming! You don't have to push!

21:25.210 --> 21:26.110
- I'm coming! You don't have to push!

22:56.120 --> 22:57.080
(Shadow Stalker)

22:57.080 --> 22:59.650
(Shadow Stalker)
Next time, "Shadow Stalker."

22:59.650 --> 23:01.120
(Shadow Stalker)
